Oh, maybe we should make this like a really chill episode then.

00:00:51.260 --> 00:00:53.560
Maybe this one, like, you know, like, I don't care.

00:00:53.720 --> 00:00:55.520
Yeah, I'd say that's more my stuff right now.

00:00:55.520 --> 00:00:58.240
It's a rampage, but like, baby, we're here.

00:00:58.480 --> 00:00:59.680
We're recording a podcast.

00:00:59.820 --> 00:01:00.900
It's like, whatever.

00:01:00.900 --> 00:01:02.520
We do it on our own time.

00:01:03.380 --> 00:01:04.820
Okay. I like that.

00:01:04.940 --> 00:01:09.800
Mike, I just, I don't, I'm sorry that I'm throwing a wrench into your thing right now.

00:01:09.800 --> 00:01:14.840
But was that the same exact back of the box as the last game?

00:01:14.840 --> 00:01:16.700
Yeah, it was.

00:01:16.940 --> 00:01:21.860
I didn't change it in the show notes because we're just so, we're just so lax this episode.

00:01:23.100 --> 00:01:25.080
You know, like, yeah, right now.

00:01:25.240 --> 00:01:27.160
Yeah, yeah, exactly.

00:01:27.580 --> 00:01:34.700
Okay. Yeah. No, I did screw up there if you want me to be honest, but I'm not going to change it because I feel like rampage would also be something you would want to prepare for.

00:01:34.820 --> 00:01:40.960
If two kaiju ever came to your city and attacked it, you know, you would want to be prepared for that kind of thing.

00:01:41.140 --> 00:01:45.460
So this video game could help you theoretically prepare for a kaiju attack.

00:01:45.460 --> 00:01:47.540
Yeah, a Pacific Rim, if you will.

00:01:48.940 --> 00:01:50.720
Yeah, I'm a fan.

00:01:50.840 --> 00:01:52.060
I'm a fan. Okay, yeah.

00:01:52.160 --> 00:01:53.960
So that's where we should probably start, right?

00:01:54.060 --> 00:01:59.920
Because this whole thing is based around, like, Godzilla and other kaiju monster films.

00:02:00.160 --> 00:02:02.760
And, you know, I have a lot of experience.

00:02:03.040 --> 00:02:05.320
Yeah, King Kong. I have a lot of experience in that area.

00:02:05.320 --> 00:02:07.020
But like, what about you guys?

00:02:07.140 --> 00:02:08.020
Sean, you want to start us off?

00:02:08.120 --> 00:02:10.480
Like, what's your kaiju familiarity?

00:02:11.600 --> 00:02:15.940
Yeah, when you say experience in that area, I'm kind of like scratching my head what you mean by that.

00:02:16.020 --> 00:02:19.620
But I guess you mean like just kaiju media.

00:02:20.380 --> 00:02:28.240
Yeah, and if you're a fan of like just the original Gojira or if you're like, hey, I like the campiness of Godzilla versus Mechagodzilla as well.

00:02:28.240 --> 00:02:42.980
You know, I actually was one of the few people that was introduced to Godzilla with the Matthew Broderick movie, which I later found out made me an outcast.

00:02:42.980 --> 00:02:45.060
So I didn't hate that movie.

00:02:45.080 --> 00:02:49.520
But in retrospect, I know that it wasn't the best place to go into it.

00:02:50.080 --> 00:02:52.540
I do like a lot of the Godzilla movies.

00:02:52.820 --> 00:02:55.960
And I also really loved Pacific Rim.

00:02:56.220 --> 00:03:01.800
So yeah, I'd say I've got a I've got a healthy kaiju appreciation.

00:03:02.560 --> 00:03:03.780
And what about you, Sam?

00:03:04.620 --> 00:03:08.920
My Godzilla experience goes back to Godzilla 2000.

00:03:09.900 --> 00:03:11.440
I think that's what it was called.

00:03:11.840 --> 00:03:14.300
Yeah, I didn't see it because I was a little kid.

00:03:14.780 --> 00:03:20.280
And but I did get this toy that was one of the Godzilla eggs, I think.

00:03:20.780 --> 00:03:22.780
And it comes out of the egg.

00:03:23.160 --> 00:03:24.680
I think that's part of it.

00:03:24.920 --> 00:03:27.020
Or I'm getting mixed up with Jurassic Park 3.

00:03:27.020 --> 00:03:28.880
Yeah, it's like the Matthew Broderick movie.

00:03:29.360 --> 00:03:33.380
Yeah, they put all the eggs in Madison Square Garden.

00:03:33.620 --> 00:03:37.460
Yeah. It wasn't Godzilla 2000, but that was the Japanese one.

00:03:37.460 --> 00:03:40.940
Godzilla 2000. Yeah, he goes up against Orca?

00:03:41.720 --> 00:03:43.120
I forget that. That I don't know.

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:48.140
Yeah, I forget the name. There's a good chance of mixing this up with a toy from Jurassic Park 3.

00:03:48.460 --> 00:03:49.580
But that's...

00:03:50.240 --> 00:03:55.600
There's a good chance that everything you've ever talked about on this podcast was actually in reference to Jurassic Park 3.

00:03:55.600 --> 00:03:57.840
Thing is, I've never even seen Jurassic Park 3.

00:03:58.440 --> 00:03:59.320
It's underrated.

00:04:00.140 --> 00:04:02.780
I just got the one egg toy, but it may be Godzilla.

00:04:02.960 --> 00:04:03.940
I'm pretty sure it's Godzilla.

00:04:04.100 --> 00:04:14.160
Anyway, so never actually seen a Godzilla movie, but I did watch Pacific Rim in college my sophomore year on Halloween when I wasn't feeling well.

00:04:14.280 --> 00:04:15.480
And I didn't want to go out.

00:04:16.320 --> 00:04:24.640
Sean, you and I set the world record for a number of times to fall asleep in a movie theater with Godzilla the 2014 film.

00:04:24.640 --> 00:04:28.680
Yeah, Godzilla 2014 I was excited for.

00:04:28.980 --> 00:04:37.580
I don't know if we both got pilled or if we got roofied or if we just really hated that movie.

00:04:37.780 --> 00:04:40.800
But I think we fell asleep at the same exact time.

00:04:40.900 --> 00:04:41.760
It was kind of romantic.

00:04:42.500 --> 00:04:46.740
Yeah, and every time I woke up, I fell asleep within another five seconds.

00:04:47.240 --> 00:04:53.360
One day, one day they will learn that nobody cares about what happens to the humans in these films.

00:04:53.680 --> 00:04:54.720
I know. Yeah.

00:04:56.500 --> 00:05:01.080
You'd think that they've got, what was that, Ken Watanabe?

00:05:01.840 --> 00:05:03.760
Yes. You got Bryan Cranston.

00:05:04.540 --> 00:05:05.380
For two minutes.

00:05:05.580 --> 00:05:11.260
For two minutes, but they didn't, I don't think they really, they didn't tell you that it was only going to be for two minutes.

00:05:11.260 --> 00:05:17.680
No, they did not. They reeled you in with this cast and they just, nobody wrote their characters, so.

00:05:18.460 --> 00:05:21.840
And they looked at that and they said, you know what would fix this in the sequel?

00:05:22.120 --> 00:05:23.880
Get the coach from Friday Night Lights.

00:05:24.040 --> 00:05:25.200
Have him be the star instead.

00:05:27.540 --> 00:05:28.980
He's been in other movies too.

00:05:30.280 --> 00:05:31.220
He's not just the coach.

00:05:31.460 --> 00:05:33.960
He's just the coach. Clear eyes, full hearts, can't lose.

00:05:34.140 --> 00:05:36.460
And we can't lose because we're going to continue on with this episode.

00:05:36.460 --> 00:05:38.140
We're going to talk about the video game now.

00:05:39.220 --> 00:05:40.180
Rampage, that is.

00:05:40.700 --> 00:05:44.160
You know, the NES version got a bug to pick already with this thing.

00:05:44.780 --> 00:05:48.100
You know, it starts with just two monsters instead of three.

00:05:48.820 --> 00:05:51.800
That's true. That's annoying and we'll get into that.

00:05:51.940 --> 00:05:56.460
But I would love it if, Sam, if you could just give me like, pretend I don't know anything about Rampage.

00:05:56.580 --> 00:05:59.260
Give me the easiest overview of what I'm doing in this game.

00:05:59.940 --> 00:06:05.360
You are a giant monster and your goal is to climb buildings and destroy them.

00:06:05.360 --> 00:06:08.060
And you gain health by eating people.

00:06:08.680 --> 00:06:12.060
And you try to avoid getting shot by the military.

00:06:12.920 --> 00:06:18.200
And eating things that you don't like, like toilets that makes you sick.

00:06:18.400 --> 00:06:21.400
And chemicals, which are in buildings sometimes.

00:06:22.580 --> 00:06:25.380
And once all the buildings are destroyed, that's it.

00:06:25.440 --> 00:06:27.940
And then the level's over. And smash as much stuff as you can.

00:06:28.240 --> 00:06:30.480
Yeah, I think that's pretty clear.

00:06:31.040 --> 00:06:34.860
I'd be surprised if people aren't familiar with Rampage.

00:06:35.020 --> 00:06:37.620
It's one of those games that like, I never played at an arcade.

00:06:37.880 --> 00:06:39.300
But I just knew about it.

00:06:39.380 --> 00:06:41.420
Like looking at it, like you saw it, you know?

00:06:41.800 --> 00:06:44.320
I actually, I played it a lot in the arcade.

00:06:44.960 --> 00:06:47.480
I played this game a lot on the N64 actually.

00:06:48.220 --> 00:06:49.700
Oh, the sequel, right?

00:06:49.840 --> 00:06:53.160
There was Rampage and Rampage World Tour.

00:06:53.420 --> 00:06:55.340
I think there were two of them.

00:06:55.460 --> 00:06:57.760
Because there was one where you could play as a weird lobster guy.

00:06:58.480 --> 00:06:59.740
Okay, that's cool.

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:01.660
Yeah. More monsters, the better.

00:07:01.940 --> 00:07:04.680
There's World Tour and then I believe there's Universal Tour.

00:07:04.940 --> 00:07:08.180
Which is obviously a much bigger deal to be going across the universe.

00:07:08.440 --> 00:07:09.800
I've played both of them.

00:07:09.940 --> 00:07:12.580
I rented them from video stores for the N64.

00:07:13.520 --> 00:07:16.440
And I remember really, really liking them.

00:07:16.660 --> 00:07:17.960
And they were a blast.

00:07:18.600 --> 00:07:22.680
Yeah, I played these in the arcades whenever I saw it.

00:07:22.820 --> 00:07:24.020
I think it was World Tour.

00:07:24.260 --> 00:07:25.180
Maybe not the original.

00:07:26.740 --> 00:07:33.200
But to me it just seemed like, it was a weird, it was a different kind of game.

00:07:33.380 --> 00:07:40.100
Like it wasn't like go and beat up the bad guys and continue to perform against other things.

00:07:40.100 --> 00:07:42.300
It was just like, destroy the environment.

00:07:42.360 --> 00:07:45.420
And I really liked that it was different in that way.

00:07:45.420 --> 00:07:55.660
And just, I always had like a thing for destructible scenery in games.

00:07:55.720 --> 00:07:56.940
And I guess this is where it started.

00:07:57.300 --> 00:08:06.140
So I have fond memories of playing as Lizzie in whatever arcade I was in when I was a child.

00:08:06.940 --> 00:08:08.820
So we all played as Lizzie.

00:08:08.940 --> 00:08:10.180
That's just our preferred character?

00:08:10.400 --> 00:08:11.360
Yes. Yeah.

00:08:11.540 --> 00:08:13.480
Pretty much. Yeah. I don't know.

00:08:13.660 --> 00:08:17.840
Something about the King Kong character is just like cliched.

00:08:18.120 --> 00:08:21.180
Right? To be a giant ape just like climbing buildings.

00:08:21.260 --> 00:08:22.560
Is the lizard not?

00:08:23.680 --> 00:08:26.900
Well, the lizard doesn't quite scream like, you know.

00:08:27.140 --> 00:08:29.540
Godzilla to me is more dinosaur than lizard.

00:08:30.140 --> 00:08:34.180
Well, so is Lizzie. Like I know he's not, but I'm saying he doesn't look like a lizard.

00:08:34.180 --> 00:08:36.380
He looks more like a dinosaur.

00:08:36.860 --> 00:08:39.160
A big dinosaur. He's a big dinosaur, right?

00:08:39.260 --> 00:08:40.840
So I think the lizard looks different enough.

00:08:40.920 --> 00:08:42.660
I think that's interesting. I chose Lizzie.

00:08:43.380 --> 00:08:47.080
Sean, you brought up a great point though there for a minute about, it's all about the destruction

00:08:47.080 --> 00:08:49.260
of the environment and stuff like that.

00:08:50.040 --> 00:08:55.460
And we haven't played a game where, you know, we kind of have, right?

00:08:55.480 --> 00:08:56.820
If you think about like Pac-Man, right?

00:08:56.820 --> 00:08:59.720
The idea is to just clear off the screen with all the dots, right?

00:08:59.800 --> 00:09:01.100
And we said that was satisfying.

00:09:01.420 --> 00:09:06.780
And in this one, you don't have to take care of every enemy helicopter and every person who's

00:09:06.780 --> 00:09:11.300
shooting at you. In fact, you never have to take care of any of them if you're somewhat good at dodging

00:09:11.300 --> 00:09:12.240
that stuff, I suppose.

00:09:12.860 --> 00:09:17.060
But the real objective of the game is just to smash up all the buildings on the screen

00:09:17.060 --> 00:09:17.960
until they collapse.

00:09:18.520 --> 00:09:23.020
And my question now, to make this full circle, is that part satisfying?

00:09:23.020 --> 00:09:26.700
We talked about how that's satisfying in games where it's clear objective, you do it.

00:09:26.700 --> 00:09:30.520
And then the screen moves on to the next thing and you just repeat that process.

00:09:30.620 --> 00:09:33.320
Is that a satisfying process to destroy these buildings?

00:09:34.260 --> 00:09:41.240
I'll say that it's not as satisfying as I know it can be from playing another Rampage

00:09:41.240 --> 00:09:49.360
game. And I think that it's pretty clunky when your jump is very fixed and the jumping doesn't

00:09:49.360 --> 00:09:54.420
feel great. You can't do that thing in regular Rampage where you're at the top of the building and

00:09:54.420 --> 00:09:58.540
you're hitting it from the top to destroy it, which I really missed.

00:09:58.960 --> 00:10:05.080
I thought that the movement was really clunky, but I think that destroying the buildings is

00:10:05.080 --> 00:10:09.720
still satisfying, even in this weird lo-fi NES way.

00:10:10.340 --> 00:10:12.000
Yeah, I agree with that.

00:10:12.000 --> 00:10:26.940
I think that while it's definitely lo-fi and it's not the arcade version, I do have a lot

00:10:26.940 --> 00:10:28.500
of bones to pick with this version.

00:10:28.500 --> 00:10:30.960
It still scratches that itch to an extent.

00:10:30.960 --> 00:10:38.540
Yeah, it's satisfying in the sense of the objective is clear of the number of buildings on the

00:10:38.540 --> 00:10:41.980
screen, right? It's usually four or five buildings at a time.

00:10:42.160 --> 00:10:44.140
You knock one of them down at a time.

00:10:44.140 --> 00:10:47.500
I don't think you can take down multiple buildings at once or anything like that.

00:10:48.020 --> 00:10:51.620
And then those buildings collapse and that's just the screen fades out.

00:10:51.760 --> 00:10:55.580
And now you're greeted with the next level in another city in that same state.

00:10:55.580 --> 00:11:03.260
You know, what's not satisfying about this gameplay loop is that the process of destroying

00:11:03.260 --> 00:11:07.460
these buildings is awkward on this NES version of the game.

00:11:07.680 --> 00:11:11.400
Sam, you mentioned the jump and I do think that's a big part of it.

00:11:11.500 --> 00:11:19.100
But even just the actual punching of the buildings when you're scaling them and stuff like that,

00:11:19.100 --> 00:11:25.980
there isn't a sound effect registered for when you do like initial damage but don't quite

00:11:25.980 --> 00:11:27.420
destroy the building.

00:11:27.780 --> 00:11:31.120
And that really bothered me for some reason that like you could punch the building but

00:11:31.120 --> 00:11:35.200
it's like you need to punch it maybe two or three times on certain buildings to get like

00:11:35.200 --> 00:11:40.400
a hole in them. But you wouldn't necessarily like know that and there's no good feedback for that there.

00:11:40.560 --> 00:11:43.820
So it just kind of feels like you're not doing anything and you kind of just keep scaling

00:11:43.820 --> 00:11:48.000
up and then you get bombarded with whatever the helicopters and people are shooting at you

00:11:48.000 --> 00:11:51.900
and you have to kind of like either accept that punishment as you're trying to continue

00:11:51.900 --> 00:11:55.780
destroying the building or you need to like say, all right, I need to get off of this building

00:11:55.780 --> 00:11:58.380
because there's too much going on here and move to something else.

00:11:59.740 --> 00:12:04.060
And scaling the buildings themselves is weird because you don't get to just say like, okay,

00:12:04.120 --> 00:12:05.080
I'm next to the building.

00:12:05.080 --> 00:12:07.720
I'm just going to hit up on my D-pad and start climbing it.

00:12:07.900 --> 00:12:12.620
You have to be facing the appropriate direction of the building from the side at which you're

00:12:12.620 --> 00:12:18.180
approaching it. So if you want to scale the left side, you have to be facing it, you know, from the right

00:12:18.180 --> 00:12:19.640
and then being able to scale up.

00:12:19.720 --> 00:12:21.840
You can't just be within the vicinity of it.

00:12:21.880 --> 00:12:24.100
I guess that somewhat makes sense.

00:12:24.240 --> 00:12:27.160
But for an arcade game, that's supposed to be pretty simple and straightforward.

00:12:27.820 --> 00:12:29.720
The logic there kind of annoyed me.

00:12:29.980 --> 00:12:32.980
Yeah, I'd say that it's it's it's pretty sticky.

00:12:33.320 --> 00:12:34.200
It's it's there.

00:12:34.300 --> 00:12:35.320
The controls feel sticky.

00:12:35.320 --> 00:12:41.000
And the fact that there isn't a lot of feedback when you're near damage that you've already

00:12:41.000 --> 00:12:45.040
caused kind of also makes it feel a little flat.

00:12:45.060 --> 00:12:51.440
But I think it's sort of mixed in terms of the control of this game, because while like

00:12:51.440 --> 00:12:54.940
your jump. It's sort of like at a fixed arc.

00:12:56.300 --> 00:13:05.000
You can it unlike a lot of games with a that takes care of like jumping and interacting

00:13:05.000 --> 00:13:10.260
while you're in the middle of a jump, you can like climb on.

00:13:10.340 --> 00:13:15.320
You can just stick to a building if you're if you're hitting up while you're in the jump.

00:13:15.500 --> 00:13:21.620
So you can you can get a little better at it and you can start to get a feel for those

00:13:21.620 --> 00:13:24.740
controls, even though they do feel a little sticky.

00:13:25.920 --> 00:13:31.160
And I also think that a pro for the control scheme in this is that while you're attached

00:13:31.160 --> 00:13:36.360
to a building, you can punch in pretty much any direction that you want.

00:13:36.460 --> 00:13:39.560
You can punch up. You can punch to the left, to the right.

00:13:39.700 --> 00:13:44.000
And it has nothing to do with which you're not like locked to the building that you're

00:13:44.000 --> 00:13:44.860
that you're on.

00:13:44.940 --> 00:13:49.700
You can also hit buildings that are close enough to the one that you're on.

00:13:49.860 --> 00:13:54.820
And you can strategically get on the correct building so that you have access.

00:13:54.940 --> 00:13:58.500
To the other ones and maybe kill three birds with one stone.

00:13:59.360 --> 00:14:05.020
And I also would while I think it might be defending it a little too much.

00:14:05.240 --> 00:14:07.580
You are a giant monster.

00:14:07.900 --> 00:14:10.300
And I maybe they should feel a little weighty.

00:14:10.300 --> 00:14:17.180
I mean, it's I guess this just feels bad, but I can see that like a more sluggish control

00:14:17.180 --> 00:14:22.220
scheme could make this feel like you are bigger than a person.

00:14:22.560 --> 00:14:25.740
No, I completely agree with with that aspect of it.

00:14:25.800 --> 00:14:30.220
And that brings up a good point that I wanted to talk about is just, you know, even forget

00:14:30.220 --> 00:14:31.360
gameplay for a second.

00:14:31.580 --> 00:14:33.180
Just being the monster, right?

00:14:33.320 --> 00:14:36.900
Like that is that is who you are in this game.

00:14:37.060 --> 00:14:43.720
There's a choice there to be this really powerful kaiju monster attacking the buildings and just

00:14:43.720 --> 00:14:46.580
kind of, you know, being an unstoppable force.

00:14:47.700 --> 00:14:53.480
One, did you feel that you were this all powerful, unstoppable force?

00:14:53.840 --> 00:14:59.160
And two, you know, to go off of what Sean said there at the end about being this big, clunky

00:14:59.160 --> 00:15:08.000
thing. Would you have preferred if instead of instead of being this big monster in the sense of like

00:15:08.000 --> 00:15:14.820
the bulkiness of it, would you have rather been something else destroying buildings, you know,

00:15:14.880 --> 00:15:19.080
that would have complemented a different a different side of things if you could have it that way?

00:15:19.620 --> 00:15:21.320
Huh? That's an interesting question.

00:15:21.680 --> 00:15:29.440
Are you saying like a small like with very agile like monster?

00:15:30.020 --> 00:15:35.900
Yeah. Like imagine if, you know, I think about like Hulk, the Incredible Hulk had a game on the

00:15:37.080 --> 00:15:40.700
PS2, I think it was like, I think it was called like Ultimate Destruction or something like that.

00:15:40.800 --> 00:15:44.200
And it was literally a game where you just play as the Hulk and you're just trying to like just

00:15:44.200 --> 00:15:45.520
cause a lot of damage.

00:15:45.660 --> 00:15:50.280
And that was a really fun game to play, mostly because of environmental destruction.

00:15:50.280 --> 00:15:55.000
Like you mentioned earlier, Sean, that's just like a fun thing to do, especially in like 3D games.

00:15:55.320 --> 00:15:58.400
